```code
def read_records(lines):
    for line in lines:
        if "=" not in line:
            continue
        key, value = line.split("=", 1)
        yield key.strip(), value.strip()
def chunks(items, size):
    batch = []
    for item in items:
        batch.append(item)
        if len(batch) == size:
            yield batch
            batch = []
    if batch:
        yield batch
print(list(chunks(range(7), 3)))
```

Prints [[0, 1, 2], [3, 4, 5], [6]]. Python 3.12+ also provides itertools.batched(items, 3), which yields tuples.

