Also: do not log full request headers; log URLs without query-string secrets; redact serial numbers or customer data if logs leave the lab; test your redaction (Project 1’s test_redact_hides_secrets).

Automation tools take input from config files, command lines and the systems they test. Validate:

- configuration (types, ranges, required keys) at start-up — fail fast (Projects 1–3);

- command allow-lists for anything executed remotely (Project 2’s `APPROVED_COMMANDS);`

- file names derived from external data (safe_name() in Project 2 prevents path traversal like ../../etc/passwd in artifact names);

- data received from devices — treat it as untrusted: check lengths before indexing bytes, handle malformed JSON, cap sizes.

