How it works:

- **Simulated suite** runs on any Linux agent for every change; JUnit results feed Jenkins test trends; HTML report and logs are archived.

- **Lab smoke** runs only when RUN_LAB is ticked, on an agent labelled bmc-lab with network access to the BMC, holding a lock on the BMC (Lockable Resources) so only one job uses it; passwords come from Jenkins credentials as masked environment variables.

- pytest exits non-zero on failures, which fails the sh step; the junit step in post { always } still records results. Teams that prefer “unstable” over “failed” for test failures can add || true and rely on the junit step’s result marking.

