The Credentials plugin stores secrets encrypted on the controller. Each credential has:

- a **kind**: secret text, username with password, SSH username with private key, secret file, certificate;

- an **ID** (e.g. bmc-lab-01-creds) that pipelines reference: choose meaningful, stable IDs; a **scope**: Global (usable by jobs) or System (only for Jenkins itself, e.g. agent • connections);

- a **domain** and/or **folder**: credentials stored in a folder are available only to jobs in that folder: a simple and effective way to limit who can use them.

